0,Southwest Tanna language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwest_Tanna_language,"Southwest Tanna is a dialect chain spoken on the southwestern coast of Tanna Island in Vanuatu. Lynch names three major dialects: Nivhaal in the north-west of the language area, Nivai in the south-west, and Nelpwaai in the north-east.","Tanna, Southwest",Austronesian
1,"Tanna, Southwest Language (NWI)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/nwi/,"Southwest Tanna is a stable indigenous language of Vanuatu. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Tanna, Southwest",Austronesian
